  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "389 Directory Server is an LDAP version 3 (LDAPv3) compliant server. The base packages include the Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) server and command-line utilities for server administration. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* 389-ds-base: 389-ds-base: pre-auth LDAP filter injection in CleanAllRUV status check (CVE-2026-11770)\n\n* 389-ds-base: 389-ds-base: NULL pointer dereference in deref control plugin BER parser (CVE-2026-11788)\n\n* 389-ds-base: 389-ds-base: pre-authentication stack buffer overflow in get_ruvelement_from_berval() via unbounded replica ID parsing (CVE-2026-15722)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
